  "english": "Song: \"Newly Created\" (Norasteghtsyal). Litany: \"By the Holy Cross\". [Prayer]: \"Save\" [Ketso]. Prayer: \"Guard Us\" (Pahpanya).\nMidday Introit: \"Before [Your] precious...\"\nResponse: \"The Lord has reigned\" (Lord of lords). Hymn [Tone 3/gi]: \"To You, O Christ\".\nThe morning Psalms, Reading, and Gospel are used.\nSanctus: \"Who is like the Lord\".\nIn the Evening: Mesedi: \"You have given to those who fear [You]... How they were saved.\"\n\"Holy God... who was crucified.\"\nHambartsi [Hymn at Elevating / Evening Hymn] Tone 3 [g3]: \"Wondrous Vision\" (Hrashapar tesutyun).\nLitany: \"By the Holy Cross\". [Prayer]: \"Save\". Prayer: \"Guard Us\".\n\nMonday. Of the Holy Saints: David of Dvin, and the martyrs Lambeus [Kalliopios] and Lambea [Kalliope].\nPatristic/Martyrs' Tone.\nMankunk [Magnificat/Youths] and Hambartsi [Evening Hymn] Tone 2 [bk]: \"Filled with Divine [grace]\".\nMidday Psalm 5: \"Lord, as with a shield\".\nProverbs 13:1 to verse 7: \"with great wealth\".\nProphet Micah 7:18: \"Who is a God\" to verse 20: \"from the days of old\".\nThe Apostle: Hebrews 12:1: \"Therefore we also\" to verse 7: \"God deals with you\".\nAlleluia of the Martyrs, in the Tone.\nGospel according to Luke 13:22: \"And he went through the cities\" to verse 30: \"and the last shall be first\".\n\nTuesday. Of the Holy Saints: Eustace [Eustathius], and his wife Theopiste, and their two sons, and the holy virgins Hermione and Nectarina.\nPatristic/Martyrs' Tone.\nMidday Psalm 39 [40]: \"With patience I waited\".\nProphet Jeremiah, Lamentations 3:22: \"The mercies of the Lord\" to verse 56: \"my voice\".\nThe Apostle: 2 Timothy 3:10: \"But you have followed\" to verse 15: \"in Christ Jesus\".\nAlleluia of the Martyrs, in the Tone.\nGospel according to Matthew 5:1: \"And seeing [the multitudes]\" to verse 12: \"who were before you\".\n\nWednesday. Tone of Repentance.\nMidday Psalm: \"Save Your servant\".\nThe Apostle: 2 Corinthians 12:10: \"Therefore I take pleasure\" to verse 18: \"did we not walk in the same steps?\".\nAlleluia, in the Tone.\nGospel according to Mark 10:35: \"And there came [to Him]\" to verse 45: \"in place of many\".\n\nThursday. Of the Holy Princes: Sahak and Hamazasp.\nPatristic/Martyrs' Tone.\nMankunk [Youths] and Hambartsi [Evening Hymn] Tone 4 [dk]: \"Brave ones\".\nMidday Psalm 124 [125]: \"Those who trust in the Lord\".\nProverbs (Wisdom of Solomon) 6:11: \"For those who kept\" to verse 21: \"leads to the kingdom\".\nProphet Jeremiah 17:7: \"Thus says the Lord\" to verse 8: \"fruit\".\nThe Apostle: Romans 8:18 [rendered as 8:10]: \"For I consider\" to verse 26: \"our weakness\".\nAlleluia of the Martyrs, in the Tone.\nGospel according to John 16:1: \"These things I have spoken to you\" to verse 4: \"I was with you\".\n\nFriday. Tone of Rest.\nMidday Psalm 97 [98]: \"All have seen\".\nThe Apostle: 2 Corinthians 12:19: \"Again, do you think\" to verse 13:4: \"by the power of God\".\nAlleluia of the Fast, in the Tone.\nGospel according to Mark 11:15: \"And they came to Jerusalem\" to verse 26: \"your transgressions\".\n\nSaturday. Of the Holy Seventy-Two Disciples of Christ.\nArakheal [Blessing/Hymn] Tone 4 [dk]: \"Heavenly Wisdom\" with its canons.\nMankunk [Youths]: \"Apostles of God\".\nMidday Psalm 18 [19]: \"Through all the earth\".\nProverbs (Wisdom of Solomon) 9:9: \"The Lord is with you\" to verse 10:2: \"to hold all\".\nBook of Exodus 15:27: \"And the children [of Israel] came\" to verse 16:1: \"and to Sinai\".\nThe Apostle: 2 Corinthians 2:14: \"But thanks be to God\" to verse 3:3: \"on tablets of human hearts\".\nAlleluia: \"Through all the earth\".\nGospel according to Luke 10:1: \"After these things\" to verse 9: \"the kingdom of God\".\nIn the Evening: \"Joyful Light\" (Luys Zvart).\nMesedi: \"I loved\".\nHambartsi [Evening Hymn] Tone 3 [gi]: \"Holy are You, Lord\" and \"We entreat You\".\nLitany: \"Let us ask\". [Prayer]: \"Save\" [Ketso].\nPrayer: \"King of Peace\".\n\nFourth Sunday after the Holy Cross.\nTone 4 [dz]: \"O praised...\".\nMetsatsooghtsyun [Magnificat]: \"O most supreme Mother of God\".\nMidday Psalm 64 [65]: \"To You praise is due\".\nProphet Isaiah 17:7: \"In that day\" to verse 14: \"they inherited\".\nThe Apostle: 2 Corinthians 13:5: \"Brethren, examine yourselves\" to verse 13: \"with you all, Amen\".\nAlleluia of the Resurrection, in the Tone.\nGospel according to Mark 11:27: \"They came again\" to verse 33: \"I do these things\".\n\nMonday. Of the Holy Saints: Phocas the Patriarch, and Irenaeus the follower of the Apostles.\nPatristic/Martyrs' Tone.\nMidday Psalm 131 [132]: \"Your priests\".\nProverbs 27:1.",
